Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:47:13 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 190/230] fix(matches): TopBar subtitle syncs to selected day,
 not hardcoded today
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The header used a mount-time new Date() while the DateStrip below could
move the feed days away — pick Friday and the header still said Wednesday.
The subtitle now formats selectedDay (long weekday + day + short month).
formatDayHeader was rejected deliberately: its Today/Tomorrow branches are
hardcoded English strings, which would have broken the FA acceptance, and
calendar:"gregory" keeps fa-IR on the same month/day number the strip
chips print (fa-IR's default Persian calendar renames them).

🤖 Generated with Codebuff
Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
---
 src/pages/Matches.tsx | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/pages/Matches.tsx b/src/pages/Matches.tsx
index 11910b2..f46a4a3 100644
--- a/src/pages/Matches.tsx
+++ b/src/pages/Matches.tsx
@@ -264,11 +264,17 @@ export default function Matches() {
       <ConfettiBurst trigger={burst} />
       <TopBar
         title={t("matches.title")}
-        subtitle={new Date().toLocaleDateString(lang === "fa" ? "fa-IR" : undefined, {
-          weekday: "short",
+        // The subtitle is the SELECTED day, not today: the DateStrip below
+        // can move the feed a week, and a header that stayed on Wednesday
+        // while the cards showed Friday would be the one lying. calendar:
+        // "gregory" keeps fa-IR on the same month/day number the strip's
+        // chips print (fa-IR's default Persian calendar renames them).
+        subtitle={new Intl.DateTimeFormat(locale, {
+          weekday: "long",
           day: "numeric",
           month: "short",
-        })}
+          calendar: "gregory",
+        }).format(selectedDay)}
         right={
           // The non-gesture refresh path the pull-to-refresh comment promises:
           // a real 44px button, reachable by keyboard and announced by name.
